# INVWINPU.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY, run with
# /CFG:PANEU.CFG, a settings file that is not there, on the users of
# TEST/KEYS/PANEU.REQ: a second administrator, BOSS, added by ADMIN, who
# then raised NEWBIE's level and renamed NEWBIE eight times, so that
# ADMIN's entries are more than a page.  BOSS logs in, so that the run's own
# entries, which hold its time of day, are BOSS's, whose row no
# snapshot shows selected.  From the parts of item 1, a scoped screen,
# the audit log asked for the table ITEMS lists that table's entries,
# counted: neither the item nor, later, that filter reaches the other
# list.  Admin > Users shows beside the users, with no setting asking
# for it, what the first, ADMIN, did, newest first: the new names and
# the level change.  F6 gives them the focus, counted though they are
# more than a page, and ESC gives it back.  DOWN twice, and the entries
# are CLERK's; DOWN, and NEWBIE, who never logged in, has none.  F6
# gives the empty entries the focus, and ESC gives it back.  On CLERK
# again F6 shows the entries' own Record menu, where ENTER, INS and DEL
# do nothing; ESC goes back to the users.  CLERK's full name edited and
# saved leaves CLERK's entries as they were, the change being BOSS's.
# View > Pane beside the list shows the users alone, CLERK still
# selected, and once more with the entries; the splitter dragged left
# narrows the users.  CLERK, at level 2, finds Admin > Users grayed.
# The end by Exit: TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/PANEU.CFG is the settings file it
# leaves.  TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINPU.SNP is its snapshot; TEST/framchk.py
# checks it.
T BOSS
K TAB
T Boss1986
K ENTER ALT-C P ALT-A A
T ITEMS
K ENTER
S AUDIT
K ESC ESC ALT-A U
S USERS
K F6
S LONG
K ESC DOWN DOWN
S FOLLOW
K DOWN
S NONE
K F6
S EMPTY
K ESC UP F6
S TRAIL
K ENTER INS DEL
S READONLY
K ESC
S MASTER
K CTRL-E TAB TAB
T Stock Clerk
K ENTER
S EDITED
K ALT-V P
S ALONE
K ALT-V P
S BOTH
M 220 DOWN MID
M 220 MOVE MID -60 0
M 220 UP MID -60 0
S DRAGGED
K ALT-F L STAB
T CLERK
K TAB
T Clerk1986
K ENTER ALT-A
S LEVEL2
K ESC ESC ALT-F X
